<article class="env-remark" id="0AJM">
        
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AJM">Remark <span data-tag="0AJM">87.28.1</span> <span class="named">(Universal property restricted power series)</span>.</a> Let $A \to C$ be a continuous map of complete linearly topologized rings. Then any $A$-algebra map $A[x_1, \ldots x_ r] \to C$ extends uniquely to a continuous map $A\{ x_1, \ldots , x_ r\}  \to C$ on restricted power series. </p>
